\[ 18 \text{ mph} + 12 \text{ mph} = 30 \text{ mph} \]

Since they start biking towards each other at the same time, the time taken for them to meet is the same. Let $x$ be the distance from City $A$ where they meet. Then, the distance from City $B$ is $45 - x$ miles.

