\]
Adding these together:
\[
\frac{36}{216} + \frac{12}{216} + \frac{1}{216} = \frac{49}{216}
\]

Thus, the probability that at some point the running total equals 3 is \(\frac{49}{216}\). The fraction is already in its simplest form, so \(m = 49\) and \(n = 216\). Therefore, \(m + n = 49 + 216 = 265\).

\[
\boxed{265}
\] 48%|████▊     | 19/40 [49:26<47:12, 134.87s/it] 50%|█████     | 20/40 [49:59<34:48, 104.42s/it]
