   \text{Area} = \pi \times (4)^2 = 16\pi
   \]

2. The middle ring is between radii 4 and 6. Its area is:
   \[
   \text{Area} = \pi \times (6)^2 - \pi \times (4)^2 = 36\pi - 16\pi = 20\pi
   \]

3. The outer ring is between radii 6 and 7. Its area is:
   \[
   \text{Area} = \pi \times (7)^2 - \pi \times (6)^2 = 49\pi - 36\pi = 13\pi
   \]

The areas of the regions are 16π, 20π, and 13π. The greatest area is 20π, and the smallest area is 13π. The difference between these areas is:
\[
20\pi - 13\pi = 7\pi
\]

Thus, the difference between the area of the region with the greatest area and the area of the region with the smallest area is \boxed{7\pi}. 45%|████▌     | 180/400 [4:38:10<3:33:12, 58.15s/it] 45%|████▌     | 181/400 [4:38:40<3:01:00, 49.59s/it]
