\[ f(q(1)) = f(b + 1) = (b + 1) - 3 \]

We know that this result must equal -3:
\[ (b + 1) - 3 = -3 \]

Simplifying this equation:
\[ b + 1 - 3 = -3 \]
\[ b - 2 = -3 \]

Solving for \( b \):
\[ b = -3 + 2 \]
\[ b = -1 \]

To verify, we substitute \( b = -1 \) back into the function \( q(x) \):
\[ q(x) = -x + 1 \]
\[ q(1) = -1 + 1 = 0 \]

Then, we apply \( f \) to this result:
\[ f(q(1)) = f(0) = 0 - 3 = -3 \]

Thus, the value of \( b \) is \(\boxed{-1}\).
