The projection of (0,6) onto the line y = (1/3)x.

The formula for projection of vector (x, y) onto line ax + by + c = 0 is:

Projection = ( (b²x - a b y - a c ) / (a² + b² ), ( -a b x + a² y - b c ) / (a² + b² ) )

But since c = 0, it simplifies to:

Projection = ( (b²x - a b y ) / (a² + b² ), ( -a b x + a² y ) / (a² + b² ) )

So, for line (1/3)x - y = 0, a = 1/3, b = -1.

