To find the sum of the coefficients of the polynomial \( g(x) \), which is defined as \( f(x - 1) \), we can use the fact that the sum of the coefficients of a polynomial \( h(x) \) is \( h(1) \). Therefore, we need to evaluate \( f(0) \) because \( g(1) = f(1 - 1) = f(0) \).

