6. Bring down another 0, making it 800. 160 goes into 800 five times (since \(5 \times 160 = 800\)), leaving no remainder.

Putting it all together, the decimal representation is 0.35625.

Thus, the decimal representation of \(\frac{57}{160}\) is \(\boxed{0.35625}\).
