\[
\frac{3 \text{ inches}}{10 \text{ miles}} = \frac{x \text{ inches}}{53.25 \text{ miles}}
\]

Cross-multiplying gives:
\[
10x = 3 \times 53.25
\]

Calculating the right side:
\[
10x = 159.75
\]

Solving for \( x \):
\[
x = \frac{159.75}{10} = 15.975
\]

To convert 15.975 into a fraction, we recognize that 0.975 is equivalent to \( \frac{39}{40} \). Thus, 15.975 can be written as the mixed number \( 15 \frac{39}{40} \), which is an improper fraction \( \frac{639}{40} \).

Therefore, the distance between the buildings on the map is:
\[
\boxed{\dfrac{639}{40}}
\]
