   \[
   2 - \log(x - 2) > 0 \implies \log(x - 2) < 2 \implies x - 2 < 10^2 \implies x < 102
   \]
   Combining these, we get \( 2 < x < 102 \).

3. The denominator \( \log(2 - \log(x - 2)) \) must not be zero:
   \[
   \log(2 - \log(x - 2)) \neq 0 \implies 2 - \log(x - 2) \neq 1 \implies \log(x - 2) \neq 1 \implies x - 2 \neq 10 \implies x \neq 12
   \]

Combining these conditions, the domain of \( f(x) \) is:
\[
(2, 12) \cup (12, 102)
\]

Thus, the domain of the function is \(\boxed{(2, 12) \cup (12, 102)}\).
