Given triangle \( \triangle ABC \) with altitudes \( \overline{AD} \) and \( \overline{BE} \) intersecting at the orthocenter \( H \). The angles \( \angle BAC = 54^\circ \) and \( \angle ABC = 52^\circ \) are given. We need to find the measure of \( \angle AHB \).

1. Calculate the third angle \( \angle ACB \):
   \[
   \angle ACB = 180^\circ - \angle BAC - \angle ABC = 180^\circ - 54^\circ - 52^\circ = 74^\circ
   \]

2. Recognize that the measure of the angle formed by the orthocenter \( H \) with the vertices \( A \) and \( B \) is related to the original angles of the triangle. Specifically, \( \angle AHB \) is known to be \( 180^\circ - \angle ACB \).

3. Calculate \( \angle AHB \):
   \[
   \angle AHB = 180^\circ - \angle ACB = 180^\circ - 74^\circ = 106^\circ
   \]

Thus, the measure of \( \angle AHB \) is \(\boxed{106^\circ}\).100%|██████████| 400/400 [10:06:30<00:00, 176.14s/it]100%|██████████| 400/400 [10:06:30<00:00, 90.98s/it] 

